<%# Slice 6 (image attachments): the "Remove image only" outcome. Unlike remove (which
    always pulls the row), the claim stays active — so the row LEAVES the queue only when
    the image reports were its ONLY pending flags. If a non-image report is still pending,
    the row is REPLACED in place (its image button is gone now that image_removed_at is set,
    but the remaining reports keep it under review). The pending-count chip always refreshes.

    B4: a legacy nil-subject pending flag (subject is nullable; Slice 5 scoped the presence
    validation to :create, so pre-Slice-5 rows can still carry nil) is a REMAINING non-image
    report. `where.not(subject: IMAGE_FLAG_SUBJECTS)` compiles to NOT IN, which excludes
    NULLs — so the nil row must be OR'd back in, or its hujah's row would be dropped from the
    queue while the pending-count chip (which counts it) still shows it. %>
<% if @hujah.flags.pending.where.not(subject: Hujah::IMAGE_FLAG_SUBJECTS)
      .or(@hujah.flags.pending.where(subject: nil)).exists? %>
  <%= turbo_stream.replace dom_id(@hujah, :moderation_item) do %>
    <%= render "moderation/flagged_hujah", hujah: @hujah %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <%= turbo_stream.remove dom_id(@hujah, :moderation_item) %>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "moderation-pending-count" do %>
  <%= render "moderation/pending_count" %>
<% end %>
